From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry Zhao <jerryz123@berkeley.edu>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 22:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Size ExceptionsSm trap signatures for expanded walks

The medeleg generator now exercises every misaligned and access-faulting
instruction for each delegation value.  That produces roughly 1,071 traps per
file, not the 306 assumed by the stale sizing comment.  Each trap consumes up
to six XLEN-wide signature slots, so the 3,000-slot region overflows before the
walk completes.

Reserve 8,000 slots to cover the complete walk, including its privilege-mode
transitions, without relying on the trap-overflow path as a normal terminator.

---
 .../src/testgen/priv/extensions/ExceptionsSm.py          | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/generators/testgen/src/testgen/priv/extensions/ExceptionsSm.py b/generators/testgen/src/testgen/priv/extensions/ExceptionsSm.py
--- a/generators/testgen/src/testgen/priv/extensions/ExceptionsSm.py
+++ b/generators/testgen/src/testgen/priv/extensions/ExceptionsSm.py
@@ -283,8 +283,8 @@ _CG = "ExceptionsSm_cg"
     "ExceptionsSm",
     required_extensions=["Sm"],
     extra_defines=[
         "#define BOOT_TO_MMODE",
-        "#define TRAP_SIGUPD_COUNT 3000",
+        "#define TRAP_SIGUPD_COUNT 8000",
     ],
 )
 def make_exceptionssm(test_data: TestData) -> list[TestChunk]:
@@ -324,7 +324,8 @@ def make_exceptionssm(test_data: TestData) -> list[TestChunk]:
     test_chunks.append(test_data.end_test_chunk())
 
     # medeleg only exists with S-mode; walk it from M-, S- and U-mode.  One file per mode: each walk
-    # records 306 trap signatures of up to 6 words, ~1.8k words of the TRAP_SIGUPD_COUNT area.
+    # records roughly 1,071 trap signatures of up to 6 words.  Reserve enough XLEN-wide slots for
+    # the complete walk and its privilege-mode transitions in the TRAP_SIGUPD_COUNT area.
     for mode_tag, priv_mode in (("mode_m", 3), ("mode_s", 1), ("mode_u", 0)):
         tc = test_data.begin_test_chunk(f"medeleg_{mode_tag[-1]}")
         tc.code.append("#ifdef S_SUPPORTED")
